const guides = {
  "citizen-tsuyosa-nj0150-56e": {name:"Citizen TSUYOSA", reference:"NJ0150-56E", type:"Integrated-bracelet automatic · CAD 500–700", price:"CAD 650", facts:[["40 mm","Stainless-steel case"],["8210","Automatic calibre"],["42 hours","Power reserve"]], lead:"A modern automatic with an integrated bracelet, black sunray dial and a confident 40 mm profile: a polished route into everyday mechanical style.", why:"The TSUYOSA combines the appeal of an automatic movement with practical daily specifications: sapphire crystal, a date display, a steel bracelet and 50 m water resistance. It feels more deliberate than a fashion watch while remaining accessible enough to be worn often.", fits:"Use it for a modern office, dinners, city weekends and travel. The black dial keeps the design versatile; the bracelet brings a cleaner, more architectural finish than a leather-strap alternative.", limits:"At 40 mm with an integrated bracelet, it has real wrist presence. It is a refined daily automatic, not a rugged tool watch; its 50 m rating suits normal daily exposure and swimming but does not make it a diver.", specs:"40 mm silver-tone stainless-steel case and integrated bracelet; black sunray dial; anti-reflective sapphire crystal; Citizen calibre 8210 automatic movement; three hands and date; 42-hour power reserve; hacking seconds; 50 m water resistance; 138 g.", source:"https://www.citizenwatch.com/ca/en/product/NJ0150-56E.html", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-gear-train-v1.png"},
  "hamilton-jazzmaster-viewmatic-h32515555": {name:"Hamilton Jazzmaster Viewmatic", reference:"H32515555", type:"Swiss dress automatic · CAD 700–2,000", price:"CAD 1,120", facts:[["40 mm","Stainless-steel case"],["H-10","Automatic calibre"],["80 hours","Power reserve"]], lead:"A restrained Swiss automatic with silver dial, sapphire crystal and an 80-hour reserve: built for people who want traditional watchmaking without theatrical styling.", why:"The Viewmatic takes a classic dress-watch formula and makes it practical. Its H-10 automatic movement offers a long reserve, while the open caseback gives a quiet reminder of the machinery behind the dial. The silver dial and leather strap keep it composed.", fits:"This is strongest with tailoring, knitwear, a relaxed jacket or an office wardrobe that leans more refined than sporty. It is an excellent choice for dinners, milestones and everyday situations where a field or dive watch would feel too casual.", limits:"Its 50 m water resistance is practical but not a reason to treat it as a swim or sports watch. A leather strap also needs more care than steel or rubber, especially around moisture.", specs:"40 mm stainless-steel case; silver dial; sapphire crystal; Hamilton H-10 automatic movement; 80-hour power reserve; Nivachron balance spring; open caseback; Super-LumiNova; calf-leather strap; 50 m water resistance.", source:"https://www.hamiltonwatch.com/en-ca/h32515555-jazzmaster-day-date-auto.html", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-balance-v1.png"},
  "citizen-series8-831-nb6050-51w": {name:"Citizen Series8 831", reference:"NB6050-51W", type:"Japanese luxury automatic · CAD 700–2,000", price:"CAD 1,595", facts:[["40 mm","Faceted steel case"],["8310","Automatic calibre"],["100 m","Water resistance"]], lead:"A sharper Citizen automatic with a faceted steel case, textured green dial and mechanical focus: sport-luxury without a borrowed identity.", why:"The Series8 831 sits above entry-level integrated-bracelet watches with a more angular case, a textured dial and a purpose-built automatic calibre. It gives the collection a stronger visual point of view while keeping the practical confidence of sapphire crystal and 100 m water resistance.", fits:"It works with a modern office wardrobe, dinner plans, travel and smart weekends. The green dial adds personality, but the steel bracelet and geometric case keep the overall effect controlled rather than flashy.", limits:"This is a noticeable, design-led watch rather than a discreet dress piece. Its integrated bracelet shape deserves a try-on if possible, because bracelet geometry affects fit as much as case diameter.", specs:"40 mm silver-tone faceted stainless-steel case and matching bracelet; green textured dial; sapphire crystal; Citizen calibre 8310 automatic movement; three hands and date; magnetic resistance; 100 m water resistance.", source:"https://www.citizenwatch.com/ca/en/product/NB6050-51W.html", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-plate-v1.png"},
  "cartier-santos-wssa0096": {name:"Cartier Santos de Cartier", reference:"WSSA0096", type:"Luxury automatic dress watch · CAD 10,000+", price:"CAD 12,200", facts:[["39.8 mm","Large steel case"],["1847 MC","Automatic calibre"],["100 m","Water resistance"]], lead:"An icon with real aviation history: Cartier's square Santos in steel, powered by an automatic movement and finished with two interchangeable straps.", why:"The Santos is valuable because its form is immediately recognizable without being loud. Its square case, exposed screws and integrated bracelet deliver a design language that works equally well with a jacket or a clean weekend outfit. Cartier pairs that historic silhouette with its 1847 MC automatic movement, sapphire crystal and practical 100 m water resistance.", fits:"Choose it for work, dinners, travel and formal events where you want a watch with cultural weight rather than a purely technical tool. The steel bracelet is polished and architectural; the supplied leather strap lets the same watch feel calmer and more traditional.", limits:"This is a large, square watch, so its 39.8 mm measurement wears differently from a round watch of the same nominal width. Try the proportions if possible. Its luxury price also means service, insurance and buying only through an authorized source matter.", specs:"Large stainless-steel case, 47.5 x 39.8 mm and 9.38 mm thick; black dial; sapphire crystal; Cartier calibre 1847 MC self-winding mechanical movement; steel SmartLink bracelet plus interchangeable nubuck alligator strap; QuickSwitch system; 100 m water resistance.", source:"https://www.cartier.com/en-ca/watches/collections/santos-de-cartier/santos-de-cartier-watch-CRWSSA0096.html", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-gear-train-v1.png"},
  "grand-seiko-evolution-9-slgw003": {name:"Grand Seiko Evolution 9", reference:"SLGW003", type:"Japanese luxury manual dress watch · CAD 10,000+", price:"CAD 15,000", facts:[["38.6 mm","Brilliant Hard Titanium"],["9SA4","Manual high-beat"],["80 hours","Power reserve"]], lead:"A compact hand-wound Grand Seiko that turns high-beat engineering and quiet finishing into a serious dress-watch proposition.", why:"The SLGW003 demonstrates how much presence can live in a restrained watch. Its 9SA4 movement runs at a high beat rate while offering an 80-hour reserve, and the thin 38.6 mm titanium case makes the technical achievement feel controlled rather than oversized. It rewards the owner who enjoys winding a watch and noticing how its finishing changes in different light.", fits:"This is for tailored days, quiet dinners, collecting with intention and anyone who prefers refinement over immediate brand signalling. The dark crocodile strap and compact proportions keep it elegant; the unusual titanium finish gives the case more character than plain polished steel.", limits:"It is splash resistant, not a sports or swim watch. It requires daily or regular manual winding, which is part of its appeal but not for everyone. Its price also puts fit, after-sales support and an authorized retailer relationship ahead of impulse buying.", specs:"38.6 mm Brilliant Hard Titanium case, 45 mm lug-to-lug and 9.95 mm thick; box-shaped sapphire crystal with inner anti-reflective coating; see-through caseback; hand-wound Grand Seiko calibre 9SA4; approximately 80-hour reserve; crocodile leather strap; splash resistance.", source:"https://www.grand-seiko.com/ca-en/collections/slgw003g", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-balance-v1.png"},
  "zenith-chronomaster-revival-a384": {name:"Zenith Chronomaster Revival", reference:"El Primero A384", type:"Swiss automatic chronograph · CAD 10,000+", price:"CAD 13,600", facts:[["37 mm","Revival steel case"],["El Primero","Automatic chronograph"],["5 Hz","High-beat movement"]], lead:"A compact chronograph that brings Zenith's 1969 El Primero story into a modern luxury collection without losing its original character.", why:"The A384 Revival is a direct route into one of watchmaking's most important automatic chronograph families. Its value is not only visual: the El Primero is celebrated for pairing an automatic chronograph with a high-frequency movement. The restrained 37 mm case keeps the design elegant, while the chronograph function gives the watch a genuine purpose beyond decoration.", fits:"Wear it when you want a vintage-informed piece that still feels considered: creative work, dinners, travel, collector meetups and relaxed tailoring. Its smaller case works especially well for people who want a high-end chronograph without the bulk often associated with the category.", limits:"A chronograph has more visual and mechanical complexity than a simple three-hand watch, so it is not the cleanest choice for strict formalwear. Its historical design is intentional and distinctive; buy it because the proportions and story speak to you, not solely for a famous movement name.", specs:"Chronomaster Revival El Primero A384 collection model; steel revival case; automatic high-frequency El Primero chronograph movement; 5 Hz regulating rate; 1/10th-second chronograph heritage; contemporary official Canadian reference price shown by Zenith's Chronomaster collection.", source:"https://www.zenith-watches.com/en_ca/products/chronomaster", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-plate-v1.png"},
  "hamilton-khaki-field-expedition-h70315130": {name:"Hamilton Khaki Field Expedition", reference:"H70315130", type:"Swiss automatic field watch · CAD 700–2,000", price:"CAD 1,560", facts:[["41 mm","Steel field case"],["H-10","Automatic calibre"],["100 m","Water resistance"]], lead:"A genuine modern field watch with an internal compass bezel, long reserve and enough polish to leave the trail behind and enter the city.", why:"The Expedition takes Hamilton's field-watch language beyond nostalgia. Its rotating compass design, screw-down crown, sapphire crystal and 80-hour H-10 calibre give it practical credibility, while the steel bracelet and textured dial make it more composed than a purely tactical piece.", fits:"It works for travel, daily movement, casual offices and weekends outdoors. The black dial and steel bracelet are deliberate enough for a relaxed jacket or knitwear, without asking you to dress like an expedition member.", limits:"At 41 mm it has greater presence than a traditional compact field watch. The compass scale is a useful tool but needs basic sun-navigation knowledge; buy it for the entire field-watch package, not the feature alone.", specs:"41 mm stainless-steel case, 11.5 mm thick; black textured dial with Super-LumiNova; sapphire crystal; screw-down crown; H-10 automatic calibre with 80-hour reserve and Nivachron balance spring; internal compass design; steel bracelet; 100 m water resistance.", source:"https://www.hamiltonwatch.com/en-ca/h70315130-khaki-field-expedition-auto.html", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-gear-train-v1.png"},
  "longines-hydroconquest-41": {name:"Longines HydroConquest", reference:"41 mm automatic", type:"Swiss automatic diver · CAD 2,000–10,000", price:"CAD 2,050", facts:[["41 mm","Steel dive case"],["Automatic","Swiss movement"],["300 m","Water resistance"]], lead:"A Swiss automatic diver with a clear tool-watch purpose, robust 300 m rating and enough refinement to work outside the water.", why:"HydroConquest gives the dive category a true Swiss tool-watch option rather than a style-only approximation. Its unidirectional bezel, screw-in crown and 300 m water resistance are paired with an automatic movement and a restrained steel case, balancing function with a more polished everyday finish.", fits:"Use it for travel, sport, weekends, casual offices and holidays near water. It is a strong one-watch choice for someone whose daily routine moves between active time and smarter plans, and who prefers a real diver's capability.", limits:"A dive bezel, bolder markers and 41 mm case make it sportier than a dress watch. Its 300 m specification is serious, but water use still demands sensible care of the crown, gaskets and bracelet over time.", specs:"41 mm stainless-steel automatic HydroConquest; unidirectional bezel; screw-in crown and caseback; Swiss automatic movement; sapphire crystal; 300 m water resistance. Official Longines Canada collection reference price shown for the steel automatic model.", source:"https://www.longines.com/en-ca/watches/conquest/hydroconquest", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-balance-v1.png"},
  "tudor-ranger-m79950-0001": {name:"TUDOR Ranger", reference:"M79950-0001", type:"Swiss automatic field watch · CAD 2,000–10,000", price:"CAD 4,025", facts:[["39 mm","Satin steel case"],["MT5402","COSC automatic"],["70 hours","Power reserve"]], lead:"A purpose-built Swiss field watch whose calm black dial and COSC manufacture movement make it capable without becoming costume-like.", why:"The Ranger succeeds because it is restrained. Its fully brushed 39 mm case, legible domed dial and 70-hour manufacture movement are all about durability and precision rather than decorative excess. It carries a real expedition lineage while staying clean enough to be a daily luxury watch.", fits:"It is at home with denim, outerwear, travel and informal work settings. Choose it if you want one confident, low-maintenance luxury watch that reads as informed rather than flashy, especially for a smaller or medium wrist.", limits:"The brushed, tool-oriented finish is intentionally less formal than a polished dress watch. It has no rotating dive bezel, chronograph or date complication; that simplicity is central to its appeal, but it should be a conscious choice.", specs:"39 mm satin-finished steel case, 12 mm thick; domed sapphire crystal; black domed dial; TUDOR Manufacture Calibre MT5402, self-winding and COSC certified; approximately 70-hour reserve; 100 m water resistance; steel bracelet with rapid-adjustment clasp.", source:"https://www.tudorwatch.com/en/watches/ranger/m79950-0001", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-plate-v1.png"},
  "longines-dolcevita-l5-767-4-71-6": {name:"Longines DolceVita", reference:"L5.767.4.71.6", type:"Swiss automatic dress watch · CAD 2,000–10,000", price:"CAD 2,650", facts:[["28.2 × 47 mm","Rectangular steel case"],["Automatic","Self-winding movement"],["45 hours","Power reserve"]], lead:"A rectangular Swiss automatic that gives the Dress filter a more architectural, formal option than the usual round three-hand watch.", why:"DolceVita is a good reminder that luxury watch design is not all about sport cases. Its rectangular profile, silver flinqué dial and automatic movement provide a classic, composed alternative for someone who wants elegance without resorting to a generic fashion watch.", fits:"It is strongest with tailoring, dinners, formal events and quieter office wardrobes. The steel bracelet makes it easier to wear daily than a precious leather strap, while the proportion and dial keep the mood clearly dressy.", limits:"Its 3 bar water resistance is for ordinary daily contact, not swimming. A rectangular case also has a longer visual footprint than a round watch, so try it on or compare lug-to-lug dimensions before purchasing.", specs:"28.20 × 47.00 mm stainless-steel case; silver flinqué dial; scratch-resistant sapphire crystal; self-winding mechanical movement at 28,800 vibrations per hour; date display; up to 45-hour reserve; steel bracelet; 3 bar water resistance.", source:"https://www.longines.com/en-ca/p/watch-longines-dolcevita-l5-767-4-71-6", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-balance-v1.png"},
  "hamilton-intra-matic-auto-chrono-h38446732": {name:"Hamilton Intra-Matic Auto Chrono", reference:"H38446732", type:"Swiss automatic chronograph · CAD 2,000–10,000", price:"CAD 3,410", facts:[["40 mm","Black PVD steel case"],["H-31","Automatic chronograph"],["60 hours","Power reserve"]], lead:"A 1968 racing idea brought forward in black PVD, orange accents and a proper Swiss automatic chronograph movement.", why:"The Intra-Matic is useful because it gives the Chronograph category a more editorial, design-led choice. Its historical racing language has a real connection to Hamilton's Chrono-matic story, but the all-black finish and orange details make the result feel current rather than like a museum reissue.", fits:"Wear it for evenings, creative work, travel and casual tailoring. It is a conversation watch for someone who wants a recognisable silhouette and a usable chronograph, without the heavy visual language of many modern racing watches.", limits:"The 40 mm PVD case and orange details make it more expressive than a quiet dress chronograph. It belongs in a rotation that includes a simpler daily watch, and black coating deserves care to keep its finish looking its best.", specs:"40 mm black PVD stainless-steel case; black dial with orange accents; perforated strap; automatic Hamilton H-31 chronograph movement; sapphire crystal; vintage racing-inspired design; official Canadian reference price for H38446732.", source:"https://www.hamiltonwatch.com/en-ca/h38446732-american-classic-auto-chrono.html", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-plate-v1.png"},
  "longines-spirit-zulu-time-l3-802-4-53-2": {name:"Longines Spirit Zulu Time", reference:"L3.802.4.53.2", type:"Swiss automatic GMT · CAD 2,000–10,000", price:"CAD 4,550", facts:[["39 mm","Steel GMT case"],["L844","COSC automatic GMT"],["72 hours","Power reserve"]], lead:"A refined 39 mm GMT that makes a credible companion for changing time zones, rather than a travel-themed accessory.", why:"The Zulu Time carries a direct connection to Longines' 1925 dual-time wristwatch and backs the story with useful modern engineering: a chronometer-certified automatic movement, silicon balance spring, ceramic bezel and 72-hour reserve. It is a travel watch that remains restrained enough for daily wear.", fits:"It is ideal for work trips, frequent travel, airport days and anyone who has family or colleagues in another time zone. The black dial and leather strap keep the character polished; the GMT hand brings a layer of real function without the visual busyness of a chronograph.", limits:"A GMT adds another display to learn and set. Its 10 bar water resistance is versatile, but the leather strap is not the most natural choice for regular swimming or high heat. Check whether the strap or steel-bracelet version suits your routine.", specs:"39 mm stainless-steel case and ceramic bidirectional bezel; black matte dial with Super-LumiNova; sapphire crystal with multi-layer anti-reflective treatment; screw-in crown; self-winding L844 GMT movement with silicon balance spring; COSC certified; date; 72-hour reserve; 100 m water resistance; leather strap.", source:"https://www.longines.com/en-ca/p/watch-longines-spirit-zulu-time-l3-802-4-53-2", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-gear-train-v1.png"},
  "tissot-seastar-1000-t1208071105100": {name:"Tissot Seastar 1000", reference:"T120.807.11.051.00", type:"Swiss automatic diver · CAD 700–2,000", price:"CAD 995", facts:[["40 mm","Steel dive case"],["Powermatic 80","Swiss automatic"],["300 m","Water resistance"]], lead:"A compact automatic diver with 300 m water resistance and 80-hour reserve, built for people who want real capability without a giant case.", why:"This Seastar earns its place because it addresses a common gap: an automatic Swiss diver that is substantial but still wearable at 40 mm. The Powermatic 80 movement, sapphire crystal, screw-down crown and 300 m rating make it functional enough to be more than a sporty visual choice.", fits:"Use it for holidays, water, active weekends and a casual wardrobe that benefits from a more technical watch. Its steel bracelet and restrained black dial also keep it useful for weekday routines where a larger, louder diver would feel excessive.", limits:"A diver's bezel and luminous markers will always read sportier than a dress watch. Though it is 40 mm, it remains 12.48 mm thick; people who prefer very thin watches should try its profile before deciding.", specs:"40 mm 316L stainless-steel case, 12.48 mm thick; black dial; sapphire crystal with anti-reflective coating; unidirectional bezel; screw-down crown and caseback; Powermatic 80 Swiss automatic with Nivachron balance spring; date; 80-hour reserve; quick-release steel bracelet; 300 m water resistance.", source:"https://www.tissotwatches.com/en-ca/T1208071105100.html", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-balance-v1.png"},
  "tudor-black-bay-58-m7939a1a0nu-0001": {name:"TUDOR Black Bay 58", reference:"M7939A1A0NU-0001", type:"Swiss automatic diver · CAD 2,000–10,000", price:"CAD 5,350", facts:[["39 mm","Steel diver case"],["MT5400-U","METAS automatic"],["200 m","Water resistance"]], lead:"A compact modern diver with a calm 39 mm silhouette, heritage cues and a technical movement that makes it much more than a vintage-looking watch.", why:"Black Bay 58 is compelling because its proportions make a serious dive watch feel everyday wearable. This current steel-bracelet version pairs the familiar 39 mm case with the METAS-certified MT5400-U manufacture calibre, delivering a more modern technical foundation beneath its restrained design.", fits:"It is a natural choice for daily wear, travel, water, weekends and casual offices. Its small-to-medium dimensions allow it to sit beneath sleeves more easily than many divers, while the bracelet gives enough polish for dinners or a relaxed jacket.", limits:"It is still a diver: its bezel, luminous dial and robust build make it sportier than a dress watch. Water resistance does not eliminate the need for regular pressure checks, especially if it is actually used in water.", specs:"39 mm steel case and steel bracelet; unidirectional dive bezel; sapphire crystal; TUDOR Manufacture Calibre MT5400-U, self-winding and METAS certified; approximately 65-hour reserve; screw-down crown; 200 m water resistance.", source:"https://www.tudorwatch.com/en/watches/black-bay-58/m7939a1a0nu-0001", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-plate-v1.png"},
  "grand-seiko-sbgm221": {name:"Grand Seiko Elegance GMT", reference:"SBGM221", type:"Japanese automatic GMT dress watch · CAD 2,000–10,000", price:"CAD 6,700", facts:[["39.5 mm","Steel dress case"],["9S66","Automatic GMT"],["72 hours","Power reserve"]], lead:"An ivory-dial GMT that turns a second time zone into something elegant enough for a suit, not just a travel tool.", why:"The SBGM221 shows how GMT can be composed rather than aggressive. Grand Seiko pairs an ivory dial, blue-steel 24-hour hand and box-shaped sapphire crystal with its 9S66 automatic movement, creating a watch for people who travel but do not want to wear a sports instrument every day.", fits:"It is best for travel, client meetings, weddings, dinners and collectors who value craft and proportion. The leather strap and warm dial make it a natural companion to tailoring, knitwear and quieter combinations.", limits:"Its leather strap and dress-watch construction do not make it the best option for swimming or high-impact use. The GMT display asks for a little setup knowledge; its benefit is clarity across two time zones, not complication for its own sake.", specs:"Grand Seiko Elegance Collection; ivory flat dial; 39.5 mm stainless-steel case; box-shaped sapphire crystal; blue-steel 24-hour hand; Grand Seiko calibre 9S66 self-winding GMT movement; approximately 72-hour reserve; date display; leather strap; official Canadian reference price shown by Grand Seiko.", source:"https://www.grand-seiko.com/ca-en/collections/elegance/e3", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-gear-train-v1.png"},
  "tissot-gentleman-t1658071105100": {name:"Tissot Gentleman", reference:"T165.807.11.051.00", type:"Swiss automatic dress watch · CAD 700–2,000", price:"CAD 1,050", facts:[["38 mm","Steel everyday case"],["Automatic","Swiss movement"],["80 hours","Power reserve"]], lead:"A compact Swiss automatic that keeps the dress-watch idea useful for the office, the weekend and the moments in between.", why:"The Gentleman is a strong foundation watch because it does not ask its owner to choose between formal and everyday. The 38 mm steel case, black dial and bracelet are restrained, while sapphire crystal, an exhibition back and an 80-hour reserve give the watch practical mechanical substance.", fits:"Use it for work, dinners, travel and first serious-watch ownership. Its proportion is especially compelling for smaller to medium wrists or anyone who wants a watch that disappears under a shirt cuff without feeling overly formal.", limits:"Its 100 m rating gives it real daily confidence, but it is not a dedicated dive watch. The design is intentionally quiet; buyers seeking a dramatic bezel, bright colour or visible complication should look elsewhere.", specs:"38 mm 316L stainless-steel case; black dial; scratch-resistant sapphire crystal with anti-reflective coating; see-through caseback; Swiss automatic movement; up to 80-hour reserve; interchangeable quick-release steel bracelet; 100 m water resistance.", source:"https://www.tissotwatches.com/en-ca/T1658071105100.html", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-balance-v1.png"},
  "tissot-ballade-t1564081109300": {name:"Tissot Ballade", reference:"T156.408.11.093.00", type:"Swiss COSC automatic dress watch · CAD 700–2,000", price:"CAD 1,380", facts:[["39 mm","Fluted steel case"],["COSC","Certified automatic"],["80 hours","Power reserve"]], lead:"A green-dial Swiss automatic with a fluted bezel and chronometer certification: more character than a plain three-hand watch, without losing restraint.", why:"Ballade brings a genuinely useful layer of precision to an elegant daily watch. Its Powermatic 80 movement is COSC certified, while the 39 mm case, Roman indexes and fluted bezel give the design a more traditional character without becoming costume-like.", fits:"It works for a client meeting, a dinner, a wedding or a polished everyday wardrobe. The green dial is expressive enough to distinguish the watch, yet the steel bracelet makes it easier to use often than a precious leather-only alternative.", limits:"The fluted bezel and Roman numerals are deliberate dress details, so it will not suit someone who wants a pure tool-watch look. Its 10.98 mm profile is still relatively slim, but fit and bracelet comfort should always be checked in person.", specs:"39 mm 316L stainless-steel case, 10.98 mm thick; green dial with Roman indexes; sapphire crystal with double-sided anti-reflective coating; see-through caseback; Powermatic 80 COSC automatic movement with Nivachron balance spring; date; 80-hour reserve; quick-release steel bracelet; 100 m water resistance.", source:"https://www.tissotwatches.com/en-ca/T1564081109300.html", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-gear-train-v1.png"},
  "citizen-promaster-dive-bn0191-55l": {name:"Citizen Promaster Dive", reference:"BN0191-55L", type:"ISO diver · CAD 200–499", price:"CAD 476", facts:[["44 mm","Steel diver case"],["Eco-Drive","Light-powered"],["200 m","ISO dive rating"]], lead:"A blue-dial ISO diver with a steel bracelet and light-powered movement: a practical entry into real water capability without the upkeep of a battery change.", why:"This Promaster earns its place through honest tool-watch credentials. It pairs a unidirectional timing bezel, screw-down crown and 200 m ISO-rated water resistance with Eco-Drive technology, which uses light as its power source. It is a sensible option for someone whose lifestyle includes water, travel and hard daily use.", fits:"Wear it on holidays, active weekends and casual daily routines. The blue dial and steel bracelet are polished enough for relaxed evenings, while the functional layout stays legible in bright outdoor conditions.", limits:"At 44 mm, it has substantial wrist presence; it is not a discreet dress watch. The applied sale price can change, so readers should verify the current Canadian price and availability on Citizen before buying.", specs:"44 mm stainless-steel case and bracelet; blue dial; anti-reflective crystal; one-way rotating elapsed-time bezel; screw-back case; screw-down crown; Eco-Drive light-powered movement; 200 m ISO-compliant water resistance.", source:"https://www.citizenwatch.com/ca/en/product/BN0191-55L.html", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-plate-v1.png"},
  "hamilton-khaki-field-murph-h70405130": {name:"Hamilton Khaki Field Murph", reference:"H70405130", type:"Swiss automatic field watch · CAD 700–2,000", price:"CAD 1,410", facts:[["38 mm","Steel field case"],["H-10","Automatic calibre"],["80 hours","Power reserve"]], lead:"A genuinely wearable field watch with an uncommon origin: it began as a screen prop for Interstellar and became a modern Swiss everyday classic.", why:"Murph is more than a film reference. Hamilton puts the cinematic story around a strong daily formula: a compact 38 mm case, legible black dial, sapphire crystal and H-10 automatic movement with an 80-hour reserve. The steel bracelet version is especially versatile for people who want the field-watch idea without looking overly rugged.", fits:"It is natural with denim, knitwear, a casual office and weekend travel. The black dial and cathedral hands bring personality without shouting, making it an easy one-watch option for someone who likes stories but does not want novelty design.", limits:"Its military-inspired typography makes it more casual than a pure dress watch. It is water resistant to 100 m, but its role is daily versatility rather than diving; the absence of a date is a deliberate clean-dial choice.", specs:"38 mm stainless-steel case; black dial with Arabic numerals and cathedral hands; sapphire crystal; Hamilton H-10 Swiss automatic movement with Nivachron balance spring; approximately 80-hour reserve; steel bracelet; 100 m water resistance.", source:"https://www.hamiltonwatch.com/en-ca/h70405130-khaki-field-murph-auto.html", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-balance-v1.png"},
  "hamilton-khaki-navy-scuba-gmt-h82555330": {name:"Hamilton Khaki Navy Scuba GMT", reference:"H82555330", type:"Swiss automatic GMT diver · CAD 700–2,000", price:"CAD 1,900", facts:[["43 mm","Steel GMT case"],["Automatic GMT","Second time zone"],["300 m","Water resistance"]], lead:"A proper automatic travel-and-water watch that tracks multiple time zones without giving up the confidence of a 300 m dive-inspired case.", why:"This Hamilton makes the GMT category more useful for people whose trips include more than airports. Its red GMT hand and 24-hour bezel make another time zone readable, while the ceramic bezel, screw-down crown and 300 m rating provide real water capability. It is a large, practical sport watch with a legitimate reason for every element on its dial.", fits:"Use it for travel, beach holidays, long weekends and a casual wardrobe that can handle a bolder 43 mm case. It is especially good for someone who wants a single watch to follow home time while moving across time zones.", limits:"At 43 mm, it will dominate a smaller wrist and does not aim to be discreet. The rubber strap and bold bezel are sport-first, so it is not a substitute for a slim dress watch at formal events.", specs:"43 mm stainless-steel case; blue dial; ceramic 24-hour bezel; sapphire crystal; screw-down crown; Swiss automatic GMT movement; red GMT hand; rubber strap; 300 m water resistance.", source:"https://www.hamiltonwatch.com/en-ca/h82555330-khaki-navy-gmt-auto.html", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-gear-train-v1.png"},
  "hamilton-ventura-h24411732": {name:"Hamilton Ventura", reference:"H24411732", type:"Iconic Swiss quartz dress watch · CAD 700–2,000", price:"CAD 1,310", facts:[["32 × 50 mm","Shield-shaped steel case"],["Quartz","Precise daily movement"],["1957","Design heritage"]], lead:"A true design icon rather than a conventional watch: the Ventura's asymmetrical case has been making a statement since 1957.", why:"Ventura gives Lumio's dress selection a necessary alternative to round watches. Its unusual shield-shaped case, association with Elvis Presley and clean quartz practicality make it a deliberate style object: less about mechanical ritual and more about design history, accuracy and visual confidence.", fits:"Choose it for evening events, creative work, tailored monochrome looks and anyone whose wardrobe already has the basics covered. It works best when treated as a signature piece rather than an all-purpose sports watch.", limits:"Its geometry and 32 × 50 mm footprint wear very differently from a round watch, so trying it on matters. The quartz movement is low maintenance but will not satisfy someone whose priority is traditional mechanical engineering.", specs:"32.3 × 50.3 mm stainless-steel shield-shaped case; black dial; Swiss quartz movement; black leather strap; 50 m water resistance; Hamilton Ventura design first introduced in 1957.", source:"https://www.hamiltonwatch.com/en-ca/collection/ventura.html", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-plate-v1.png"},
  "iwc-portugieser-iw358303": {name:"IWC Portugieser Automatic", reference:"IW358303", type:"Swiss luxury automatic dress watch · CAD 10,000+", price:"CAD 10,600 before tax", facts:[["40.4 mm","Steel dress case"],["82200","IWC automatic calibre"],["60 hours","Power reserve"]], lead:"A clean, large-dial IWC that turns traditional watchmaking into a composed choice for people who prefer proportion and restraint over obvious status cues.", why:"The Portugieser is a key high-luxury dress watch because it is recognisable without being overstated. This 40 mm version combines the collection's open, nautical-inspired dial layout with IWC's calibre 82200, Pellaton winding system and a 60-hour reserve. It is a serious mechanical watch that stays remarkably calm on the wrist.", fits:"Wear it with tailoring, a business wardrobe, formal dinners and occasions where a dive bezel or busy chronograph would feel out of place. The silver dial and black alligator strap keep it timeless rather than trend-driven.", limits:"Its 3 bar water resistance is for ordinary daily contact, not swimming. A leather strap and polished dress case also need more careful use than a steel sports watch; this is a refinement-first purchase.", specs:"40.4 mm stainless-steel case, 12.3 mm thick; silver dial; convex sapphire crystal with double-sided anti-reflective coating; IWC-manufactured calibre 82200 automatic movement with Pellaton winding; small hacking seconds; 60-hour reserve; black alligator strap; 3 bar water resistance.", source:"https://www.iwc.com/ca-en/watches/portugieser/iw358303-portugieser-automatic-40", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-balance-v1.png"},
  "cartier-tank-francaise-w4ta0029": {name:"Cartier Tank Française", reference:"W4TA0029", type:"Luxury diamond quartz dress watch · CAD 10,000+", price:"CAD 12,600", facts:[["25.7 × 21.2 mm","Diamond-set steel case"],["Quartz","High-precision movement"],["1917","Tank design heritage"]], lead:"A compact Cartier Tank that treats a watch as architecture and jewellery at the same time: precision, proportion and a century of design authority.", why:"Tank Française belongs here because luxury is not only about a mechanical movement. Louis Cartier's Tank silhouette is one of the most influential forms in wristwatch design, and this diamond-set steel version adds jewellery craft while retaining the sharp dial, blue cabochon crown and integrated bracelet character that make the Tank instantly identifiable.", fits:"It is strongest at formal events, dinners, celebrations and wardrobes that value clean geometry over large sports cases. It can be worn as a discreet daily signature for someone who prefers timeless design to technical display.", limits:"This small, quartz Tank is a design and jewellery proposition, not a tool watch. Its 3 bar water resistance is not for swimming, and the diamond setting deserves more attentive use than a plain steel everyday watch.", specs:"25.7 × 21.2 mm stainless-steel case set with 22 diamonds totaling 0.70 carats; silvered sunray dial; blued-steel sword hands; sapphire crystal; synthetic blue cabochon-shaped spinel crown; steel bracelet; quartz movement; 3 bar water resistance.", source:"https://www.cartier.com/en-ca/watches/collections/tank/tank-francaise-watch-CRW4TA0029.html", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-plate-v1.png"},
  "jaeger-lecoultre-reverso-tribute-q398847j": {name:"Jaeger-LeCoultre Reverso Tribute", reference:"Q398847J", type:"Haute horlogerie manual dual-time · CAD 10,000+", price:"CAD 19,900", facts:[["47 × 28.3 mm","Reversible steel case"],["Manual","Duoface movement"],["2 zones","Second time display"]], lead:"A reversible manual-wind Reverso that makes travel, mechanics and Art Deco design feel inseparable rather than merely decorative.", why:"The Reverso is a foundational high-watchmaking form, and this Duoface version gives its reversible case a clear reason to exist. The black sunray front has small seconds, while the reverse provides a second time zone. The case's slide-and-swivel construction and hand-wound movement make the experience more tactile than a conventional round automatic.", fits:"Choose it for formal travel, dinners, collecting and people who value design history and mechanical interaction. Its rectangular profile makes it distinct with tailoring, while the dual-time display is useful when work or family crosses time zones.", limits:"It is a refined manual dress watch, not a swimming or sport option. The rectangular proportions wear longer than a round case, and manual winding asks for an intentional daily ritual. Try the fit before buying.", specs:"47 × 28.3 mm stainless-steel reversible case; black sunray-brushed front dial; small seconds; reverse dual-time display; hand-wound Duoface movement; two Casa Fagliano straps in leather and leather/canvas; approximately 3 bar water resistance; CAD 19,900 official Canadian price.", source:"https://www.jaeger-lecoultre.com/ca-en/watches/reverso/reverso-tribute/reverso-tribute-duoface-small-seconds-q398847j", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-gear-train-v1.png"},
  "iwc-ingenieur-iw328901": {name:"IWC Ingenieur Automatic", reference:"IW328901", type:"Luxury sports automatic · CAD 10,000+", price:"CAD 17,600 before tax", facts:[["40 mm","Integrated steel case"],["32111","IWC automatic calibre"],["120 hours","Power reserve"]], lead:"A modern luxury-sports watch with Gérald Genta lineage, real anti-magnetic engineering and a five-day power reserve.", why:"The Ingenieur is for people who value design discipline as much as a famous logo. Its integrated bracelet and five-screw bezel reinterpret IWC's 1970s Ingenieur SL, while the soft-iron inner case, screw-down crown and 120-hour manufacture movement give the watch real technical credibility beneath its composed exterior.", fits:"It can handle a sharp office, travel, city weekends and active daily use. The black grid dial and steel bracelet make it versatile enough to be a primary luxury watch, especially for buyers who want a sports model with less obvious visual language.", limits:"This is a polished integrated-bracelet luxury watch, so its fit deserves an in-person test. Its 10 bar rating supports daily confidence, but it is not a dive watch. The official price is listed before tax.", specs:"40 mm stainless-steel case, 10.7 mm thick; black grid dial; integrated steel bracelet; convex sapphire crystal with double-sided anti-reflective coating; soft-iron inner case for magnetic protection; screw-down crown; IWC calibre 32111 automatic movement; date; 120-hour reserve; 10 bar water resistance.", source:"https://www.iwc.com/ca-en/watches/ingenieur/iw328901-ingenieur-automatic-40", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-plate-v1.png"},
  "cartier-santos-chronograph-wssa0017": {name:"Cartier Santos Chronograph", reference:"WSSA0017", type:"Luxury automatic chronograph · CAD 10,000+", price:"CAD 14,800", facts:[["43.3 mm","Steel and ADLC case"],["1904 CH MC","Automatic chronograph"],["100 m","Water resistance"]], lead:"A Santos that treats the chronograph as part of its architecture: bold, capable and far more technical than the classic three-hand silhouette.", why:"Cartier turns its signature square case into a sporty high-luxury chronograph without losing the Santos identity. The automatic 1904 CH MC calibre, 100 m rating and two quick-change straps create a package that genuinely works beyond formal events, while the ADLC bezel and black details keep the result modern.", fits:"Wear it for travel, creative work, city evenings and a wardrobe that benefits from a large, graphic watch. It is especially strong for someone who wants Cartier design but prefers a mechanical complication with everyday robustness.", limits:"At 43.3 mm wide and 12.4 mm thick, this is an assertive watch. Its chronograph layout and ADLC details make it more expressive than a classic Tank or Portugieser, so it should be chosen for that presence.", specs:"43.3 mm steel case with ADLC bezel, 12.4 mm thick; satin-brushed silver dial; sapphire crystal; Cartier calibre 1904 CH MC automatic chronograph movement; black rubber strap plus black Gomma alligator strap; QuickSwitch interchangeability; 100 m water resistance.", source:"https://www.cartier.com/en-ca/watches/collections/santos-de-cartier/santos-de-cartier-chronograph-watch-CRWSSA0017.html", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-gear-train-v1.png"},
  "jaeger-lecoultre-master-control-q4178180": {name:"Jaeger-LeCoultre Master Control", reference:"Q4178180", type:"Perpetual calendar haute horlogerie · CAD 10,000+", price:"CAD 63,500", facts:[["39 mm","Steel ultra-thin case"],["868","Automatic perpetual calendar"],["Until 2100","Calendar accuracy"]], lead:"A 39 mm perpetual calendar that combines a serious complication, full calendar display and elegant proportions without drifting into showmanship.", why:"This Master Control represents a different level of watchmaking: the perpetual calendar tracks day, date, month and year, and is designed to remain correct through the varying length of months until 2100. Jaeger-LeCoultre puts that complexity inside a 9.2 mm steel case, while the movement's 332 components and High-Precision Guarantee Seal show that the refinement is not only visual.", fits:"This is for collecting with intent, major life milestones and formal wardrobes. Its compact 39 mm silhouette keeps the complication surprisingly wearable, while the bracelet makes it less fragile-feeling than an alligator-only dress piece.", limits:"A perpetual calendar is sophisticated and should be treated as such: setting, service and ownership are different from a simple three-hand watch. It is expensive, subtle and best for a buyer who values the mechanism itself.", specs:"39 mm stainless-steel case, 9.2 mm thick; blue-grey gradient sunray dial; automatic Jaeger-LeCoultre calibre 868 with 332 components; day, date, month, leap-year and moon-phase displays; approximately 70-hour reserve; 22K pink-gold rotor; integrated steel bracelet; High-Precision Guarantee Seal.", source:"https://www.jaeger-lecoultre.com/ca-en/watches/master-control/master-control-chronometre-perpetual-calendar-q4178180", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-balance-v1.png"},
  "grand-seiko-62gs-sbgh376": {name:"Grand Seiko 62GS", reference:"SBGH376", type:"Japanese high-beat luxury automatic · CAD 10,000+", price:"CAD 43,100", facts:[["62GS","Bezel-free case design"],["Hi-Beat","Mechanical automatic"],["CAD 43,100","Official Canadian price"]], lead:"A rare Grand Seiko 62GS that brings the Japanese house's bezel-free case architecture into its highest price territory.", why:"The 62GS matters because it was Grand Seiko's first automatic design, introduced in 1967. Its bezel-free construction lets the crystal meet the case directly, opening the dial and allowing the faceted surfaces to carry light. This SBGH376 represents that design language at a collector level, where finishing, precision and limited availability matter as much as a headline complication.", fits:"This is for collectors who value quiet finishing, Japanese watchmaking and details that reveal themselves slowly in changing light. It works best with tailoring, understated luxury and a collection built around craft rather than brand signalling.", limits:"This is an expensive specialist purchase. The exact availability and delivery timing must be confirmed with Grand Seiko or an authorized Canadian retailer before buying, and the price reflects a collector-level model rather than an entry into the brand.", specs:"Grand Seiko Heritage Collection 62GS; bezel-free case construction; high-beat mechanical automatic movement; multi-faceted case, hands and indexes; official Canadian reference price CAD 43,100. Confirm the exact reference specifications and availability directly before purchase.", source:"https://www.grand-seiko.com/ca-en/collections/heritage/h2", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-gear-train-v1.png"},
  "jaeger-lecoultre-master-control-q4168120": {name:"Jaeger-LeCoultre Master Control", reference:"Q4168120", type:"Swiss chronometer automatic · CAD 10,000+", price:"CAD 23,500", facts:[["39 mm","Steel integrated-bracelet case"],["738","COSC automatic calibre"],["70 hours","Power reserve"]], lead:"A slim 39 mm chronometer that puts date and power-reserve information into a balanced, architectural high-luxury design.", why:"This Master Control revives the Futurematic spirit through practical precision. Its Calibre 738 is COSC certified and then tested as a complete watch under Jaeger-LeCoultre's High-Precision Guarantee. The date and power-reserve displays are useful complications rather than decoration, while the integrated bracelet gives the piece a modern silhouette.", fits:"Wear it for a refined office, travel and formal occasions where you want technical depth without the visual complexity of a perpetual calendar. It suits collectors who appreciate a practical daily complication and a controlled 39 mm proportion.", limits:"This is a fine mechanical watch rather than a sport tool: its 5 bar water resistance and polished finish call for considered daily use. Buyers should verify boutique availability because high-watchmaking collections can change quickly.", specs:"39 mm stainless-steel case, 9.2 mm thick; blue-grey gradient sunray dial; integrated steel bracelet; Jaeger-LeCoultre Calibre 738 automatic movement; COSC chronometer certification; date and power-reserve displays; 70-hour reserve; 5 bar water resistance; High-Precision Guarantee Seal.", source:"https://www.jaeger-lecoultre.com/ca-en/watches/master-control/master-control-chronometre-date-power-reserve-q4168120", visual:"../watch-assets/mechanism-balance-v1.png"}
};
const key = location.pathname.split('/').pop().replace('.html','');
const item = guides[key];
document.title = item ? `${item.name} ${item.reference} | Lumio Watches` : 'Watch guide | Lumio Watches';
if (item) {
  const description = document.createElement('meta');
  description.name = 'description';
  description.content = `${item.name} ${item.reference}: independent Lumio guide with Canadian reference price, specifications, context and buying considerations.`;
  document.head.appendChild(description);
  const canonical = document.createElement('link');
  canonical.rel = 'canonical';
  canonical.href = location.href.split('?')[0];
  document.head.appendChild(canonical);
}
document.querySelector('#guide').innerHTML = item ? `<style>:root{--i:#17120f;--p:#f3eee5;--m:#77695c;--g:#b88b4a;--l:#c9b9a4}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--p);color:var(--i);font:16px/1.55 Arial}.shell{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:25px}a{color:inherit}.top,.facts,.block,.footer{border-top:1px solid var(--l)}.hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr .8fr;gap:50px;padding:75px 0 40px;align-items:center}.eyebrow{text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.16em;font-size:11px;color:var(--g)}h1,h2{font-family:Georgia,serif;line-height:1.03}h1{font-size:clamp(48px,8vw,88px);margin:14px 0}h2{font-size:30px}.lead{font-size:20px;color:#4b4037}.visual{position:relative;width:260px;height:260px;margin:auto;background:#181511;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 18px 30px #0002}.visual img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover}.visual small{position:absolute;bottom:12px;left:12px;background:#10100fcc;color:#eee9df;padding:5px 7px;font-size:8px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase}.facts,.content{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}.fact{padding:20px;border-right:1px solid var(--l)}.fact b{font:27px Georgia,serif;display:block}.fact span,.note{color:var(--m)}.content{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:30px;padding:55px 0}.block{padding:25px 0}.buy{background:#201712;color:#f5eee4;padding:42px;margin:20px 0 50px}.buy .note{color:#d6c9bb}.button{display:inline-block;background:#d9af70;color:#201712;padding:14px 20px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:bold}@media(max-width:700px){.hero,.content,.facts{grid-template-columns:1fr}.fact{border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--l)}}</style><header class="shell top"><a href="../index.html">← Lumio Watches</a></header><main class="shell"><section class="hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">${item.type}</div><h1>${item.name}<br>${item.reference}</h1><p class="lead">${item.lead}</p></div><div class="visual"><img src="${item.visual}" alt="Original watchmaking mechanism visual"><small>Watchmaking visual · not exact model</small></div></section><section class="facts">${item.facts.map(([a,b])=>`<div class="fact"><b>${a}</b><span>${b}</span></div>`).join('')}</section><section class="content"><div><section class="block"><div class="eyebrow">Why it matters</div><h2>What it brings.</h2><p>${item.why}</p></section><section class="block"><div class="eyebrow">Where it fits</div><h2>Wear it with intention.</h2><p>${item.fits}</p></section></div><div><section class="block"><div class="eyebrow">Real limits</div><h2>Know before buying.</h2><p>${item.limits}</p></section><section class="block"><div class="eyebrow">Specifications</div><h2>What you are getting.</h2><p>${item.specs}</p></section></div></section><section class="buy"><div class="eyebrow">Official Canada reference price · verified 18 Sep 2026</div><h2>${item.name} ${item.reference}: ${item.price}</h2><p class="note">Lumio does not process the purchase. Price, availability, warranty and delivery terms can change; verify the exact reference directly with the seller before buying.</p><a class="button" href="${item.source}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Check current official Canadian price →</a></section><section class="block"><div class="eyebrow">Source</div><p class="note"><a href="${item.source}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official Canadian product page: specifications, price and availability</a></p></section></main><footer class="shell footer">LUMIO WATCHES · Independent editorial discovery · Facts and price verified on the date shown; prices and availability can change.</footer>` : '<p>Guide not found.</p>';
